#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:1
#: 95a5cd7f42054522b87c64234b80ad58
msgid ""
"Dynamic DEA: Carry-overs, Intertemporal Commitments, and the Efficiency "
"of a Trajectory"
msgstr "动态 DEA：结转变量、跨期承诺与轨迹效率"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:3
#: f0674c55b3264e6fa1e979e9e4be607f
msgid ""
"A manager can often improve this year's figures by borrowing from next "
"year. Maintenance can be postponed, difficult cases can remain in a "
"queue, inventory can be run down, and experienced staff can be reassigned"
" from capability building to current delivery. An annual efficiency "
"analysis may reward every one of these choices. The organization that "
"inherits depleted capacity, unresolved work, or an empty pipeline will "
"judge them differently."
msgstr "管理者往往可以通过透支未来来改善今年的报表：推迟设备维护，把棘手病例留在队列中，消耗库存，或者把经验丰富的员工从能力建设调到当前业务交付。逐年效率分析可能会奖励所有这些选择，而接手了能力耗竭、工作积压或项目储备空缺的组织，却会作出不同评价。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:10
#: 14eea5e09c59458dade35a170556da4e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Dynamic data envelopment analysis is designed for this management "
"problem. It asks whether a sequence of operating plans remains attainable"
" when the assets, productive capabilities, and obligations passed between"
" periods are treated as part of production. Tone and Tsutsui's dynamic "
"slacks-based measure (dynamic SBM) expresses that idea with a non-radial "
"efficiency measure {cite:p}`tone2010dynamic`."
msgstr ""
"动态数据包络分析正是为这一管理问题而设计。它把期际传递的资产、生产能力与义务视为生产的一部分，考察一系列运营方案能否持续实现。Tone 与 "
"Tsutsui 提出的动态基于松弛变量的效率测度（动态 SBM），以非径向效率测度表达这一思想 "
"{cite:p}`tone2010dynamic`。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:17
#: dcdfb2c2226940989e8aa6c496d711ef
msgid ""
"The unit being appraised is no longer \"organization $o$ in year $t$.\" "
"It is organization $o$'s complete trajectory over a stated horizon. "
"Period results remain useful, but they diagnose one jointly feasible "
"plan; they are not scores from independent annual contests. This change "
"of viewpoint is the defining idea of the dynamic DEA family."
msgstr ""
"被评价单位不再是“$t$ 年的组织 $o$”，而是组织 $o$ "
"在给定期限内的完整轨迹。各期结果仍有诊断价值，但它们解释的是一个联合可行方案，并不是相互独立的年度竞赛得分。这一视角转换是动态 DEA "
"模型族的定义性思想。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:23
#: 97cdce9bb93c4aaba127c63a1c25882c
msgid "A panel becomes dynamic only when the past constrains the future"
msgstr "只有过去约束未来，面板才具有动态含义"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:25
#: e58a415c314948fb8aedf5a59ca772c4
msgid ""
"Several years of observations do not by themselves define a dynamic "
"technology. A panel is a data structure. It becomes economically dynamic "
"only when a measured condition left by one period constrains what a later"
" period can do. Capital capacity, inventories, loan quality, unfinished "
"treatments, research pipelines, maintenance backlogs, and contractual "
"obligations can all play this role."
msgstr "多年的观测本身并不能定义动态生产技术。面板只是一种数据结构；只有当某一期留下的可测状态会约束后续时期的生产机会时，它才在经济意义上成为动态系统。资本能力、库存、贷款质量、未完成治疗、研发储备、维护积压和合同义务都可能承担这一角色。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:32
#: 6c5e6203bd5c41d7b462b2de09608b3e
msgid "Two questions locate the relevant model family:"
msgstr "回答两个问题，即可判断应采用哪个模型族："

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 686dad4305cd4c32842c8ff0a02e3aa2
msgid "Does the study contain an inherited state?"
msgstr "研究中是否存在需要承接的状态？"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 30cd99a275bf4bfa9e5aba2414aef42e
msgid "Does it model processes inside the organization?"
msgstr "是否对组织内部过程建模？"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 0b9968a6c3eb44959174c2e37e4037ec
msgid "Appropriate interpretation"
msgstr "适当的解释"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 7cb85ad1f9604f8ca11c6d86cae63a12 c2181ab97adc4f7b8fd462a0faa6d645
#: dd2db126da30466d86d67f3aa42bd11a e49860ee7a34409aac8b5fddd6b1a8c7
msgid "No"
msgstr "否"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 786080b1c66e4c13b4db3fc99b26d728
msgid ""
"Static or panel DEA: years supply repeated observations or different "
"reference populations"
msgstr "静态或面板 DEA：不同年份提供重复观测，或构成不同的参照总体"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 0671b45d102d4ecf8182e2e3471a9a3c 4021180f82d84693a1f287c0ac616623
#: a89f2c8a9ca3424fb68e2861bcfebc95 c926fdff00b248f4bb50af2137ab327f
msgid "Yes"
msgstr "是"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 42061617463440ecbbb5e94218ab8118
msgid "Network DEA: internal handoffs coordinate processes within a period"
msgstr "网络 DEA：内部交付在同一期内协调各过程"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 04ce18ba27b4454b8a228e849872660f
msgid "Dynamic DEA: carry-overs coordinate the organization's plans through time"
msgstr "动态 DEA：结转变量跨期协调组织方案"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 8747f65f88a54844bbacb605cfd92a27
msgid ""
"A combined structure is required; this book develops its two core "
"ingredients separately"
msgstr "需要组合结构；本书分别讲解其两个核心组成部分"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:41
#: 7e85e42bd4574e00bb6db479782465f7
msgid ""
"This table separates production structure from productivity change. A "
"Malmquist or Luenberger index asks how operating performance or best "
"practice changes between technologies. Dynamic SBM instead asks whether "
"one complete history is efficient relative to a technology of feasible "
"histories. The ratio of two annual or dynamic efficiency scores is not "
"automatically a productivity index."
msgstr ""
"这张表区分了生产结构与生产率变化。Malmquist 或 Luenberger 指数考察不同生产技术之间的运营绩效或最佳实践如何变化；动态 SBM"
" 则考察一段完整历史相对于可行历史所构成的生产技术是否有效率。两个年度效率值或动态效率值之比，并不会自动成为生产率指数。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:48
#: 2fcab6462c4347459e740cde57722828
msgid ""
"Repeated static DEA, window DEA, and dynamic DEA therefore answer "
"different questions. Repeated static DEA treats each organization-period "
"row as a separate appraisal. Window DEA changes which rows may serve as "
"comparators. Neither imposes an accounting identity between what one "
"period leaves and the next period receives. If no defensible state "
"variable exists, calling a panel \"dynamic\" adds a label but not an "
"economic mechanism."
msgstr ""
"因此，重复静态 DEA、窗口 DEA 与动态 DEA 回答的是不同问题。重复静态 DEA 把每条“组织—时期”记录作为一次独立评价；窗口 DEA "
"改变哪些记录可以充当比较对象。二者都不会强制要求上一期留下的数量与下一期接收的数量满足核算恒等式。如果不存在站得住脚的状态变量，把面板称作“动态”只是增加标签，并没有增加经济机制。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:55
#: fffa0908a1824ccf855c0f026406e89e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The analysis below follows a **carry-over stock view**. Today's benchmark"
" cannot promise a closing stock of capacity, inventory, or backlog that "
"is inconsistent with what tomorrow's operation inherits. This is the "
"appropriate question when management must make a sequence of operating "
"plans add up across time. A different established question begins with "
"**quasi-fixed inputs**, such as generation capacity or port "
"infrastructure, that cannot be moved immediately or costlessly to a "
"desired long-run level. That approach studies whether investment and "
"input adjustment follow an efficient path once adjustment costs and "
"intertemporal substitution are recognized "
"{cite:p}`nemoto1999,nemoto2003`. A capital stock may appear in both "
"approaches, but the managerial commitments are different. A continuity "
"identity does not by itself specify investment costs, discounting, or an "
"optimal speed of adjustment. The carry-over model developed below answers"
" the first question."
msgstr ""
"下文采用**结转存量视角**。今天的标杆方案不能承诺一个期末能力、库存或积压存量，却让明天的运营方案承接一个与之矛盾的期初存量。当管理层必须使一系列运营方案在时间上前后一致时，这正是应回答的问题。另一项成熟研究问题从**准固定投入**出发，例如不能立即或无成本调整到理想长期水平的发电能力或港口基础设施；在承认调整成本与跨期替代后，该方法研究投资和投入调整是否沿有效路径进行"
" "
"{cite:p}`nemoto1999,nemoto2003`。资本存量可能同时出现在两种方法中，但二者对应的管理承诺不同。连续性恒等式本身并不能规定投资成本、贴现或最优调整速度。下文发展的结转变量模型回答的是第一个问题。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:68
#: 463179479470495aa8ab1fd7a16bddfb
msgid "Carry-over as a production commitment"
msgstr "结转变量是一项生产承诺"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:70
#: 791ebc0c04174fe298c5bb25ada2645c
msgid ""
"Consider a hospital observed for four years. Each year it uses staff and "
"beds to provide treatment, and each year it leaves some patients on a "
"waiting list. The waiting list is not merely another annual input. Cases "
"left unresolved in year 1 become obligations in year 2. A benchmark that "
"removes them from the first year's target but lets the second year behave"
" as though they were still available is not an implementable management "
"plan."
msgstr ""
"考察一家连续观察四年的医院。每年它都使用员工和床位提供治疗，也会把一些患者留在等候名单中。等候名单并非普通年度投入：第 1 "
"年尚未解决的病例会成为第 2 年的义务。如果标杆方案从第 1 年的目标中删去这些病例，却让第 2 "
"年的运营仿佛仍然承接了它们，这就不是一套可以实施的管理方案。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:77
#: 29d582dd82cb454ab16efebda6966752
msgid ""
"Other sectors have the same accounting logic. A manufacturer carries "
"productive capacity and warranty obligations; a bank carries performing "
"and non-performing loans; a university carries knowledge and degree "
"candidates; and an electricity utility carries generation capacity, fuel "
"inventories, and maintenance backlogs. In every case, the carry-over "
"records a commitment that connects current action with future "
"opportunity."
msgstr "其他行业也遵循同样的核算逻辑。制造企业结转生产能力与质保义务，银行结转正常贷款与不良贷款，大学结转知识与在读学生，电力企业则结转发电能力、燃料库存与维护积压。无论何种情形，结转变量都记录了一项把当前行动与未来机会联结起来的承诺。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:84
#: 775229aa8b314304b265f2263ae3a8b9
msgid ""
"The historical dynamic-SBM formulation uses four carry-over roles. They "
"are useful contracts between economic interpretation and benchmark "
"treatment:"
msgstr "早期动态 SBM 公式使用四类结转变量。它们构成经济解释与标杆处理方式之间有用的约定："

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 0f142ac118294de8b7fa261cf40b401e
msgid "Carry-over role"
msgstr "结转变量角色"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: ba26f9c8c92e4a0cb9bf6f407dfe3140
msgid "Economic and managerial meaning"
msgstr "经济与管理含义"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 83b0ef0b4349454daeed5edd4af88816
msgid "Treatment in the benchmark account"
msgstr "标杆账户中的处理方式"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 82aa205d7df44f19b3b5cf8c52363726
msgid "**Good / desirable**"
msgstr "**合意 / 有益**"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: f7719106ec3f42218568e58dcf83e7b5
msgid "Capacity, knowledge, reputation, or another valuable inherited condition"
msgstr "生产能力、知识、声誉或其他有价值的承接状态"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: ac3091bf028a4e718cfa85adae17d66f
msgid "A shortfall is assessed with output shortfalls"
msgstr "不足量与产出不足一并评价"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: f4faf0f495c949a2840bdfa499a6901a
msgid "**Bad / undesirable**"
msgstr "**非合意 / 有害**"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 911312d81f704b638fc90714348221c9
msgid "Backlog, debt, defective work, or another future burden"
msgstr "积压、债务、缺陷工作或其他未来负担"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 6ffe197912d44b78aea41883f2950a4d
msgid "An excess is assessed with input excesses"
msgstr "冗余量与投入冗余一并评价"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: e613379e7bd746098985cb8e3aa75de7
msgid "**Free / discretionary**"
msgstr "**自由 / 可调整**"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: ade2f94a3e4848f8965270b527a4269f
msgid "Inventory or another state that management may re-plan upward or downward"
msgstr "库存或其他可由管理者向上或向下重新规划的状态"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: e0114f0c0b0f41118b02f7f7e992e0ea
msgid ""
"A signed deviation affects feasibility but does not enter the performance"
