msgstr "可正可负的偏差影响可行性，但不进入这里使用的绩效账户"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 8196fe390a4b4a7ebda323af0aa1e4b0
msgid "**Fixed / non-discretionary**"
msgstr "**固定 / 非可控**"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 56fe85f3a28344cc8284405e9e07831e
msgid "A regulated, contractual, or inherited commitment outside current control"
msgstr "不受当前管理者控制的监管、合同或既有承诺"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md
#: 5f031c3da245400096a8b72d448eba1b
msgid "The benchmark reproduces the observation"
msgstr "标杆方案复现实际观察值"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:94
#: 4ab947a0acb84495923106b3b390552d
msgid ""
"Four annual management plans are connected by valuable capacity, harmful "
"backlog, discretionary inventory, and fixed commitments, and the entire "
"trajectory enters one performance account"
msgstr "四项年度管理方案由有价值的生产能力、有害的工作积压、可调整库存和固定承诺联结起来，完整轨迹共同进入一个绩效账户"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:99
#: 86ce2e8665b34f8aa41862d9e9037fd7
msgid ""
"Carry-overs turn a sequence of annual plans into one operating history. "
"What the benchmark leaves at the end of one period must be the condition "
"inherited by the next benchmark plan."
msgstr "结转变量把一系列年度方案转化为一段完整运营历史。标杆方案在一期末留下的状态，必须等于下一期标杆方案所承接的状态。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:104
#: c0945fdc3855427da05d22cb5edea813
msgid ""
"The labels should not replace economic reasoning. \"Good\" and \"bad\" "
"describe how a state affects future production; \"free\" and \"fixed\" "
"emphasize the scope for managerial redesign. A fuel stock may be "
"discretionary for a competitive generator but effectively fixed during an"
" emergency reserve obligation. A loan portfolio may be valuable as "
"earning capacity while some of its impaired loans are harmful burdens. "
"The analyst must explain the production role and decision rights behind "
"every declaration."
msgstr "分类标签不能代替经济分析。“合意”和“非合意”描述一种状态如何影响未来生产，“自由”和“固定”则强调管理者能够重新设计的范围。对于竞争性发电企业，燃料存量可能可自由调整；在应急储备义务下，它却可能实际上是固定的。贷款组合可能因具有创收能力而成为有价值的结转状态，其中一些减值贷款则构成有害负担。分析者必须说明每项分类背后的生产角色与决策权限。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:112
#: 05ab3bb742244034b05ba9540e9b49e8
msgid "Three tests for a defensible state account"
msgstr "建立可信状态账户的三项检验"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:114
#: 11cef8f1833f4b3da44bc8a6bb610375
msgid ""
"A variable should enter the dynamic model only when it passes three "
"practical tests. First, it must have an **intertemporal identity**. The "
"closing quantity in one plan and the inherited quantity in the next must "
"refer to the same asset, obligation, or productive condition under the "
"same measurement boundary. \"Investment spending this year\" and "
"\"capital available next year\" may be related, but they are not "
"automatically the same account. If investment creates capital with a "
"delay, loss, or depreciation rate, the study needs a transition rule that"
" represents that conversion rather than an equality borrowed for "
"convenience."
msgstr "只有通过三项实务检验的变量才应进入动态模型。第一，它必须具有**跨期同一性**。一个方案的期末数量与下一方案承接的期初数量，必须在同一测量边界下指向同一资产、义务或生产状态。“本年投资支出”和“次年可用资本”可能相关，却不会自动成为同一个账户。如果投资经过时滞、损耗或折旧才形成资本，研究需要用转换规则表示这种变化，而不是为了方便直接套用等式。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:124
#: 609e2efaac1641e48e5145007c2310b0
msgid ""
"Second, the state must have **production relevance**. Its level must "
"change what the organization can deliver or what burden it must carry. A "
"variable recorded in several years is not a carry-over merely because it "
"is persistent. Regional population, weather, or market conditions may "
"instead describe the operating environment. Treating them as stocks "
"controlled by management would confuse inherited production capacity with"
" external circumstances."
msgstr "第二，状态必须具有**生产相关性**。其水平必须会改变组织能够交付的成果，或必须承担的负担。一个变量不会仅仅因为连续多年都有记录就成为结转变量。地区人口、天气或市场条件可能描述的是运营环境；把它们当作管理者控制的存量，会混淆承接的生产能力与外部环境。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:131
#: d03bb249aff94e1883ed58218908d7d7
msgid ""
"Third, its role must match **managerial responsibility**. A maintenance "
"backlog may be harmful and partly controllable, while a legally mandated "
"service obligation may be harmful to a narrow cost account but fixed for "
"the manager being assessed. The classification should reflect the "
"decision level of the study. A board, a plant manager, and a regulator "
"can face different control sets even when they observe the same physical "
"quantity."
msgstr "第三，其角色必须符合**管理责任范围**。维护积压可能有害且部分可控，依法必须履行的服务义务对狭义成本账户而言也可能有害，但对被评价管理者却是固定的。分类应与研究采用的决策层级一致。即使董事会、工厂经理和监管者观察的是同一个实物数量，他们面对的控制集合也可能不同。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:138
#: 929a7fda87e94336b77d4aad1fda6330
msgid ""
"These tests also guard against double counting. If capital stock is a "
"carry-over, recording the same stock again as an ordinary annual input "
"can penalize one condition twice unless the production interpretation "
"clearly distinguishes capital services from the inherited asset. "
"Similarly, a waiting-list stock should not also be counted as an annual "
"undesirable output without explaining how the flow of newly unresolved "
"cases differs from the closing balance. Dynamic DEA does not remove the "
"need for production accounting; it makes inconsistencies in that "
"accounting more consequential."
msgstr ""
"这些检验还可以防止重复计算。如果资本存量已被设为结转变量，再把同一存量记作普通年度投入，可能对同一状态惩罚两次；除非生产解释明确区分了资本服务和承接资产。同理，若把等候名单存量又计作年度非合意产出，就必须说明当年新增未解决病例这一流量与期末存量有何不同。动态"
" DEA 并没有消除生产核算的必要性，反而会使核算不一致造成更严重后果。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:147
#: b1d5b1a08f4741c1a02ff4acd6e97d69
msgid ""
"The horizon is part of the state definition. A three-year review may be "
"appropriate for a service contract but too short for an infrastructure "
"asset. Beginning the horizon immediately after an unusually large "
"investment, or ending it just before a backlog must be cleared, can "
"change the apparent trajectory. Analysts should therefore justify the "
"initial and terminal dates and examine whether conclusions survive a "
"reasonable alternative horizon."
msgstr "评价期限是状态定义的一部分。三年期限对服务合同可能合适，对基础设施资产却可能过短。如果期限恰好从一次异常大规模投资之后开始，或者在必须清理积压之前结束，表面上的轨迹就会改变。因此，分析者应说明起止日期的依据，并检查结论在合理改变期限后是否仍然成立。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:154
#: 8fa130ab90af45f7aa7e68602827bf58
msgid "One peer plan per period, one feasible trajectory"
msgstr "每期一套参照方案，共同构成一条可行轨迹"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:156
#: 50cdd672b15e4c68853c48b658d261c7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Suppose $n$ organizations are observed in periods $t=1,\\ldots,T$. In "
"period $t$, $X_t$ contains ordinary inputs, $Y_t$ contains desirable "
"outputs, and $\\lambda^t\\in\\mathbb{R}_+^n$ selects a peer plan from the"
" cohort of complete trajectories. For the organization $o$ under review,"
msgstr ""
"假设在时期 $t=1,\\ldots,T$ 观察到 $n$ 个组织。在时期 $t$，$X_t$ 包含常规投入，$Y_t$ "
"包含合意产出，$\\lambda^t\\in\\mathbb{R}_+^n$ 从完整轨迹群体中选择一套参照方案。对于被评价组织 $o$，"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:161
#: 5aefeb15628b496a814c64990969b93c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"x_{ot}=X_t\\lambda^t+s_{ot}^{-},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"y_{ot}=Y_t\\lambda^t-s_{ot}^{+}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"x_{ot}=X_t\\lambda^t+s_{ot}^{-},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"y_{ot}=Y_t\\lambda^t-s_{ot}^{+}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:167
#: 36e59d5cd0ab40498abf24d06c23489d
msgid ""
"The input slack is avoidable resource use relative to the selected period"
" plan. The output slack is an attainable service shortfall. These "
"balances make each period feasible on its own, but they do not yet make "
"the periods a feasible history."
msgstr "投入松弛是相对于所选时期方案可以避免的资源使用量，产出松弛是可达到的服务不足量。这些平衡式使每一期分别可行，但尚未使各期组成一段可行历史。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:172
#: 3cbf4b5797314b5eb64d7b4a24b49696
msgid ""
"Let $C_t^\\alpha$ contain a carry-over account of role $\\alpha$. Using "
"$C$ for states keeps them distinct from within-period network links, "
"which will later use $Z$. The four period balances are"
msgstr ""
"令 $C_t^\\alpha$ 表示角色为 $\\alpha$ 的结转账户。用 $C$ "
"表示跨期状态，可以把它与期内网络联结变量区分开来；后者将在后文使用 $Z$。四类时期平衡式为"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:176
#: 50ec3e44da36488a91441cfe0fe76490
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"c_{ot}^{\\mathrm{good}}\n"
"  &=C_t^{\\mathrm{good}}\\lambda^t-s_{ot}^{\\mathrm{good}},\\\\\n"
"c_{ot}^{\\mathrm{bad}}\n"
"  &=C_t^{\\mathrm{bad}}\\lambda^t+s_{ot}^{\\mathrm{bad}},\\\\\n"
"c_{ot}^{\\mathrm{free}}\n"
"  &=C_t^{\\mathrm{free}}\\lambda^t+s_{ot}^{\\mathrm{free}},\\\\\n"
"c_{ot}^{\\mathrm{fixed}}\n"
"  &=C_t^{\\mathrm{fixed}}\\lambda^t.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"c_{ot}^{\\mathrm{good}}\n"
"  &=C_t^{\\mathrm{good}}\\lambda^t-s_{ot}^{\\mathrm{good}},\\\\\n"
"c_{ot}^{\\mathrm{bad}}\n"
"  &=C_t^{\\mathrm{bad}}\\lambda^t+s_{ot}^{\\mathrm{bad}},\\\\\n"
"c_{ot}^{\\mathrm{free}}\n"
"  &=C_t^{\\mathrm{free}}\\lambda^t+s_{ot}^{\\mathrm{free}},\\\\\n"
"c_{ot}^{\\mathrm{fixed}}\n"
"  &=C_t^{\\mathrm{fixed}}\\lambda^t.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:189
#: bb374cca589c4d98ba7792ce969a9c88
msgid ""
"Good- and bad-carry-over slacks are nonnegative. The free-carry-over "
"slack is signed because management may choose a target above or below the"
" observation. A fixed carry-over has no slack: the appraisal conditions "
"on the observed commitment."
msgstr "合意与非合意结转变量的松弛均非负。自由结转变量的松弛可正可负，因为管理层可以选择高于或低于实际观察值的目标。固定结转变量没有松弛：评价以实际承诺为条件。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:194
#: 77822d80687e490f8cb080e0283e62e0
msgid "The equation that turns these accounts into dynamic production is"
msgstr "使这些账户真正成为动态生产模型的是下面的方程："

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:196
#: 33a1a86293d2468bba49ac4aa5cda119
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"C_t^\\alpha\\lambda^t\n"
"=\n"
"C_t^\\alpha\\lambda^{t+1},\n"
"\\qquad t=1,\\ldots,T-1.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"C_t^\\alpha\\lambda^t\n"
"=\n"
"C_t^\\alpha\\lambda^{t+1},\n"
"\\qquad t=1,\\ldots,T-1.\n"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:203
#: 0b938915e7c34578998ab177f46f4762
msgid ""
"Both sides refer to the same transition account. In management language, "
"the target stock leaving period $t$ equals the stock inherited by the "
"next benchmark plan. The equation does not say that the organization's "
"observed stock must remain unchanged. It says that any redesigned path "
"must still be a path rather than a collection of incompatible annual "
"targets."
msgstr ""
"等式两端指向同一个转换账户。用管理语言说，离开时期 $t$ "
"的目标存量等于下一项标杆方案承接的存量。这并不是说组织的实际存量必须保持不变，而是说任何重新设计后的路径仍必须是一条前后连贯的路径，不能是一组彼此矛盾的年度目标。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:209
#: 95926f24467a4d64afdd8d27bbc9520f
msgid ""
"Under variable returns to scale, each period has its own convexity "
"condition,"
msgstr "在规模报酬可变下，每一期都有自己的凸性约束："

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:211
#: ffc29b6badf448b0bbbb5da594935498
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathbf 1^\\top\\lambda^t=1,\n"
"\\qquad t=1,\\ldots,T.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\mathbf 1^\\top\\lambda^t=1,\n"
"\\qquad t=1,\\ldots,T.\n"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:216
#: e640bf56af014041b762758c57d03c0c
msgid ""
"Under constant returns to scale these conditions are omitted. A single "
"horizon-wide convexity equation would not be equivalent, because every "
"period has its own peer plan."
msgstr "在规模报酬不变下，这些约束被省略。用一条覆盖整个期限的凸性方程替代并不等价，因为每一期都有自己的参照方案。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:220
#: 2490c2cdf91a4f158f2432ca8def127b
msgid "The horizon needs an explicit boundary"
msgstr "评价期限必须具有明确边界"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:223
#: eb3e6dda16714a89a69c8b458047f229
msgid ""
"The terminal-period carry-over can enter its period performance account "
"even though no continuity equation leads to an unobserved period $T+1$. "
"This does not assign a salvage value, force the terminal stock to zero, "
"or make it disappear. Studies requiring depreciation, initial stocks, "
"terminal value, or longer lags need explicitly different transition "
"equations."
msgstr ""
"终期结转变量可以进入当期绩效账户，尽管没有通往未观察时期 $T+1$ "
"的连续性方程。这既没有给终期存量赋予残值，也没有强迫其归零或使其消失。需要表示折旧、初始存量、终值或更长时滞的研究，必须明确采用不同的转换方程。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:230
#: 07720e233fa145c49bed8d7d30f31ee9
msgid "The trajectory performance account"
msgstr "轨迹绩效账户"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:232
#: 4f62a3cae610484a9699c8982015840c
msgid ""
"Dynamic SBM does more than check whether a history is feasible. It asks "
"how much avoidable burden and attainable shortfall remain in that "
"history. Let $m$ be the number of ordinary inputs, $q$ the number of "
"desirable outputs, $h_b$ the number of bad carry-overs, and $h_g$ the "
"number of good carry-overs. With equal importance within each account, "
"define"
msgstr ""
"动态 SBM 不仅检验一段历史是否可行，还要考察其中仍有多少可避免负担和可达到的成果不足。令 $m$ 为常规投入数量，$q$ "
"为合意产出数量，$h_b$ 为非合意结转变量数量，$h_g$ 为合意结转变量数量。在每个账户内部等权时，定义"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:238
#: 93a49a5b531f48dab90203dd146d830d
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"A_{ot}\n"
"&=\n"
"1-\\frac{1}{m+h_b}\n"
"\\left[\n"
"\\sum_i\\frac{s_{iot}^{-}}{x_{iot}}\n"
"+\\sum_{v\\in\\mathcal C_b}\n"
"  \\frac{s_{vot}^{\\mathrm{bad}}}{c_{vot}^{\\mathrm{bad}}}\n"
"\\right],\\\\\n"
"B_{ot}\n"
"&=\n"
"1+\\frac{1}{q+h_g}\n"
"\\left[\n"
"\\sum_r\\frac{s_{rot}^{+}}{y_{rot}}\n"
"+\\sum_{v\\in\\mathcal C_g}\n"
"  \\frac{s_{vot}^{\\mathrm{good}}}{c_{vot}^{\\mathrm{good}}}\n"
"\\right].\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"A_{ot}\n"
"&=\n"
"1-\\frac{1}{m+h_b}\n"
"\\left[\n"
"\\sum_i\\frac{s_{iot}^{-}}{x_{iot}}\n"
"+\\sum_{v\\in\\mathcal C_b}\n"
"  \\frac{s_{vot}^{\\mathrm{bad}}}{c_{vot}^{\\mathrm{bad}}}\n"
"\\right],\\\\\n"
"B_{ot}\n"
"&=\n"
"1+\\frac{1}{q+h_g}\n"
"\\left[\n"
"\\sum_r\\frac{s_{rot}^{+}}{y_{rot}}\n"
"+\\sum_{v\\in\\mathcal C_g}\n"
"  \\frac{s_{vot}^{\\mathrm{good}}}{c_{vot}^{\\mathrm{good}}}\n"
"\\right].\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:259
#: 67b89128b3774f7598a2541493615e8d
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"$A_{ot}$ is a retained-resource account: it falls when the selected plan "
"reveals avoidable inputs or harmful inherited burdens. $B_{ot}$ is an "
"output-expansion account: it rises when desirable services or valuable "
"future conditions fall short of attainable targets."
msgstr ""
"$A_{ot}$ 是资源保留账户：所选方案揭示的可避免投入或有害承接负担越多，其数值越低。$B_{ot}$ "
"是产出扩张账户：合意服务或有价值的未来状态距离可达到目标越远，其数值越高。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:264
#: cd6ab5bc82774db4a83e60928d6e9571
msgid ""
"Let $\\omega_t\\geq0$ denote declared period importance, normalized so "
"that $\\sum_t\\omega_t=1$. The horizon accounts are"
msgstr "令 $\\omega_t\\geq0$ 表示事先声明的时期重要性权重，并标准化为 $\\sum_t\\omega_t=1$。整个期限的账户为"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:267
#: ec8b634296bd4ad9a69687c24b670bff
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"A_o=\\sum_t\\omega_t A_{ot},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"B_o=\\sum_t\\omega_t B_{ot}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"A_o=\\sum_t\\omega_t A_{ot},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"B_o=\\sum_t\\omega_t B_{ot}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:273
#: afcc012e6a9441b7808401b4cbead62b
msgid "The three orientations correspond to three management mandates:"
msgstr "三种导向对应三项管理任务："

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:279
#: ef2f3b6379fb43538b0faa41be9e3dd3
msgid "Orientation"
msgstr "导向"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:280
#: e85648edda594320b67c6ec50996a0f0
msgid "Question"
msgstr "问题"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:281
#: e783b450141546329b01b00b942bbd3f
msgid "Reported trajectory efficiency"
msgstr "报告的轨迹效率"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:282
#: f4a754c91e034d7ea26b60ce63765b1e
msgid "Input"
msgstr "投入导向"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:283
#: 2c815a5d2b884aa89912f33d7f3f38c9
msgid ""
"How much ordinary resource use and harmful inherited burden can be "
"avoided while commitments are respected?"
msgstr "在遵守各项承诺的同时，可以避免多少常规资源使用和有害承接负担？"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:285
#: 4cb4e9eafa13425fa908f4df28b3d5cf
msgid "$A_o$"
msgstr "$A_o$"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:286
#: 3dc51ae71e6c471988cd35a498c33733
msgid "Output"
msgstr "产出导向"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:287
#: 229f10f351ef4d4cb40879b387acdf5f
msgid "How much service and valuable inherited capability can be expanded?"
msgstr "服务与有价值的承接能力可以扩张多少？"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:288
#: 524c76d4f29c46fa9eae9731ab458a2f
msgid "$1/B_o$"
msgstr "$1/B_o$"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:289
#: ec73919fe05c46009e7a9c1445559868
msgid "Non-oriented"
msgstr "非导向"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:290
#: 8eaf6b6177494dd8bf9b77b8607c9bc3
msgid "What joint resource and result improvement is attainable?"
msgstr "可以同时实现多大的资源改善与成果改善？"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:291
#: 156cab9f3ce845e783fae1ea1b59fd6a
msgid "$\\rho_o=A_o/B_o$"
msgstr "$\\rho_o=A_o/B_o$"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:294
#: 2d8a6e3b366f42e1a8f737dc67bf4414
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Because $B_o$ aggregates expansion accounts, output efficiency is a "
"weighted harmonic aggregation of period efficiencies $1/B_{ot}$, not "
"their arithmetic mean. Replacing it with a convenient average changes the"
" measure."
msgstr ""
"由于 $B_o$ 汇总的是扩张账户，产出效率是各期效率 $1/B_{ot}$ "
"的加权调和汇总，而不是算术平均数。用一个便于计算的平均数替代，会改变绩效测度本身。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:298
#: eb179f1cf0e548efa08990536b8feeac
msgid ""
"Period weights are management judgments, not prices learned by DEA and "
"not automatically discount factors. If recent service reliability "
"receives more weight than an early transition year, the study should "
"state why. Variable weights within the input and output accounts have the"
" same status: they express declared importance and require sensitivity "
"analysis."
msgstr ""
"时期权重是管理判断，不是 DEA "
"学到的价格，也不自动等于贴现因子。如果近期服务可靠性比早期转型期获得更高权重，研究应说明理由。投入与产出账户内部的变量权重具有同样性质：它们表达事先声明的重要性，需要进行敏感性分析。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:304
#: 7d59bd6751134179b8f1ed4f05e156b7
msgid ""
"The horizon score is the result of one joint optimization. Period scores,"
" slacks, targets, and peers explain one selected optimal trajectory. If "
"several trajectories attain the same horizon score, these lower-level "
"explanations may differ. A statement such as \"year 3 caused the "
"inefficiency\" is therefore stronger than the evidence. The defensible "
"reading is: under this jointly optimal plan, the selected diagnosis "
"locates a stated shortfall in year 3."
msgstr ""
"整个期限的效率值来自一次联合优化。各期效率值、松弛量、目标与参照单元解释的是一条选定最优轨迹。如果多条轨迹达到同一个期限效率值，这些下层解释可能不同。因此，“第"
" 3 年造成了无效率”比证据所能支持的结论更强。站得住脚的说法是：在这项联合最优方案下，所选诊断把某项明确的绩效不足定位于第 3 年。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:312
#: 93b0c8f4e83d4bb0ac9146acba9a055f
msgid "When capacity and backlog enter the same account"
msgstr "生产能力与积压进入同一个账户时"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:314
#: 455dc627689044f79309cb93e5f533f7
msgid ""
"A two-organization case makes the management meaning of the two carry-"
"over roles concrete. `dynamic_capacity_backlog` follows a Prepared "
"organization and a Strained organization over two periods. They use the "
"same ordinary input and produce the same ordinary output. What "
"distinguishes them is their operating position at the end of each period:"
" capacity is valuable for what the organization can do next, whereas "
"backlog is a burden inherited by the next managerial period."
msgstr ""
"一个包含两个组织的案例可以具体说明两类结转变量的管理含义。`dynamic_capacity_backlog` 跟踪 Prepared 组织与 "
"Strained "
"组织两个时期的表现。二者使用相同的常规投入，生产相同的常规产出；区别在于每期结束时的运营状态：生产能力对组织下一期能做什么具有价值，而积压则是下一管理期必须承接的负担。"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:275
#: f2c2f42c695c4a90809da3382a30de4f
msgid "Period"
msgstr "时期"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:275
#: 1e49ea882ce74f208fc0a67d14c4fae2 745d44397c61414fa396145ffb349151
msgid "Organization"
msgstr "组织"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:275
#: 8a44047b20974a0f9f23a3ffd9ab92f4
msgid "Ordinary resource"
msgstr "常规资源"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:275
#: fa4875c8ab4c4c879e1257b88f374724
msgid "Desirable service"
msgstr "合意服务"

#: ../../chapters/06-dynamic/dynamic-dea-carryovers-trajectories.md:275
#: 3953cd9ec366400cb170eb9e5e39eaab
msgid "Capacity"
